: Written by hand. A no-`index` dialect that nevertheless splits `arguments` across
: chunks and repeats the same `id` on each one. The guard that opens a new block on a
: "differing id" must compare against the id seen on the wire: comparing against our own
: minted ToolCallId never matches, so every fragment would start a fresh call and the
: arguments would arrive as three unparseable pieces.
